# Line endings: Unix (LF), everywhere, on every platform.
#
# 'text=auto' lets git detect text files and store them with LF in the
# repository. 'eol=lf' also checks them out with LF, so editing on Windows
# cannot reintroduce CRLF. Together they override core.autocrlf, so the
# result no longer depends on any per-machine git setting.
#
# The repo previously held a mix (most .py files CRLF, a handful LF), which
# made a one-line edit with a tool that rewrites whole files - sed -i, or a
# Python open(...,'w') without newline= - show up as a diff touching every
# line. Normalized in one pass when this file was added.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary: never inspect or convert these.
*.png binary
*.mb binary
